# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-6; the lead's fix 1). E §4.2: "Steps 0-2 are one batch at each such place: its pads at the
# start, observations and plans take from its parts together, one take per place over every outflow of the batch there
# (LANGUAGE §5.14), the batch's arrivals among its supplies"; L §5.19 A pad: "at x it is an arrival, labelled by the
# arrival rule ..., or an outflow, taken by the leaving rule, like any other".
# L §5.19 (2.1-F2): "A reading at a day's start that pads and states parts, at a place the day's first batch also
# moves, is refused (RUN-RECORD): its pad takes and arrives with the batch (ENGINE.md §4.2), so q's booked part at the
# reading is no one point's"; L §8.4 RUN-RECORD `reading <r> of <x> at <d> start pads and states parts while the day's
# first batch moves <x>` (<r> the reading's stable id, L §2.5). The parts are refused; the total stands.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == tomek then 0 else 1
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t2_day: date
input t2_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t2: tomeks
  on t2_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t2_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t2_day = 2026-03-01
  t2_amt = 50.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-03-02
  pad konto from world
  stated[konto] = 70.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start
  stated[konto] of ania = 60.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start
=== expect
q: (120.00 PLN, refused: RUN-RECORD reading stmt:stated[konto] of konto at 2026-03-01 start pads and states parts while the day's first batch moves konto, refused: RUN-RECORD reading stmt:stated[konto] of konto at 2026-03-01 start pads and states parts while the day's first batch moves konto)
  pad: konto 2026-03-01 start, pads:stmt:konto@2026-03-01 start of -30.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: t2
  cut 2026-10-01
